On RHEL (8 / 9), Docker runs as a systemd service (dockerd).
Here are the correct commands to update / reload Docker daemon.

🔄 Reload Docker daemon config (daemon.json changed)
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart docker


✔ Use this after editing:

/etc/docker/daemon.json

🔁 Restart Docker service (most common)
sudo systemctl restart docker


Check status:

sudo systemctl status docker

🔄 Reload without stopping containers (if supported)
sudo systemctl reload docker


⚠️ Not all Docker versions support reload — restart is safer.

⬆️ Update Docker Engine (RHEL 8 / 9)
1️⃣ Update Docker packages
sudo dnf update docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin

2️⃣ Restart Docker
sudo systemctl restart docker

🔍 Verify Docker version
docker version

🧠 Common troubleshooting
Docker not starting?
journalctl -u docker -xe

Enable Docker on boot
sudo systemctl enable docker


------docker-compose.override.yml-----------------

version: '3.3'

services:
  traefik:
    ports:
      # CHANGE: Map Host Port 8501 -> Container Port 8080
      - "8501:8080"
      - "8090:8090"

  cvat_ui:
    labels:
      # ROUTING FIX: Allow traffic from Load Balancer (ignores domain name mismatch)
      - "traefik.http.routers.cvat-ui.rule=PathPrefix(`/`)"
      - "traefik.http.routers.cvat-ui.entrypoints=web"

  cvat_server:
    labels:
      # ROUTING FIX: ensure API/Admin traffic goes to the backend
      - "traefik.http.routers.cvat.rule=PathPrefix(`/api/`) || PathPrefix(`/static/`) || PathPrefix(`/admin`) || PathPrefix(`/django-rq`) || PathPrefix(`/auth/`)"
      - "traefik.http.routers.cvat.entrypoints=web"
